All three claims look open on Mozilla components, as far as the searches reached:
- the per-bug selector against the best single coder, a confidence cascade and a frequency rule;
- LLM against encoder by training-count bin, at several training sizes and on later years;
- a natural-prevalence evaluation.

Reviewers would however expect comparison with BugBug's own thresholded classifier, and leakage plus label noise could blur the rare-code result.
